From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:00:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libsanitizer: add a built-in HWASan default option string

Instrumented daemons on the target have no convenient place to set
HWASAN_OPTIONS, so the runtime needs a built-in default. The string
comes in at build time as -DHWASAN_DEFAULT_OPTIONS=<opts>, unquoted;
the options are colon separated with no spaces, so they survive the
shell and make, and the runtime stringifies them.

The built-in string is parsed before __hwasan_default_options() and
before the HWASAN_OPTIONS environment variable, so both still
override it.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Cather <mattbob4@gmail.com>
---
 libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan.cpp |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan.cpp
+++ b/libsanitizer/hwasan/hwasan.cpp
@@ -129,6 +129,15 @@ static void InitializeFlags() {
   RegisterCommonFlags(&ubsan_parser);
 #endif

+  // Build-time default; __hwasan_default_options and HWASAN_OPTIONS override it.
+#ifdef HWASAN_DEFAULT_OPTIONS
+#define HWASAN_STR2(x) #x
+#define HWASAN_STR(x) HWASAN_STR2(x)
+  parser.ParseString(HWASAN_STR(HWASAN_DEFAULT_OPTIONS));
+#undef HWASAN_STR
+#undef HWASAN_STR2
+#endif
+
   // Override from user-specified string.
   if (__hwasan_default_options)
     parser.ParseString(__hwasan_default_options());
